  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Beyond Growth strategic sessions</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commons Network will organize a series of gatherings for national parliamentarians (MPs) within the European Union who are eager tofurther the discussion on postgrowth national policies in their respective countries. This series will be kickstarted during the Beyond Growth Conference (15-18 May 2023) in the European Parliament through a Roundtable Discussion Lunch event on Wednesday the 17thof May. The event in the European Parliament in May will be followed by an event in September. Beyond MPs, Commons Network will also invite national labor unions of participating countries to strengthen the cross-linkages between national labor movements and parliamentary representatives. Alongside these two gatherings in Brussels, they will organize a meeting in The Hague with MPs from the Post-growth Interparty working group in the Dutch Parliament.

Objectives
&#x2756; To provide a space for MPs across the European Union working on postgrowth policies at national level to exchange during the Beyond Growth conference in European Parliament
&#x2756; To go beyond the content of a policy agenda for postgrowth, and to focus on skills and strategies for implementing post growth policies at the national level
&#x2756; To create a network of MPs working on postgrowth policies that wouldcontribute to the integration of efforts at the national and European level.

These events aim to be a stepping stone for a potential network of parliamentarians of EU countries on post-growth policy and political debates. As such, this event would alsobe an important moment to identify the need for next events and gatherings and for such a network. Commons Network would like to further develop and co-design this in a collaboration with OxfamNovib and our partner the Green European Foundation.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Commons Network Stichting</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mission &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; VisionCommons Network is a collaboratory for the social and ecological transition. They explore new models for economy and society in order to collectively transform the system and shape a caring and just future. They bring together people and ideas and provide tools and insights for social movements, governments and civil society. A just and caring economy Commons Network aims to enhance the democratisation and social ecological transition of the economy. Instead of continuing to struggle to &quot;green&quot; growing economies, we need to get out of growth thinking and fundamentally redesign the economy. The digital dimension is a crucial part of this, as technology has come to shape our economy. Such a transition requires policies but also embracing other practices. Practices that redefine work and value creation. This means recognizing and valuing care work in the household and beyond. But also investing in the local economy and the cooperative sector where citizens unite around providing basic needs such as energy, food and shelter in a self-organizing way. This domain is also called the commons: it is a forgotten and underexposed sector in the economy alongside that of the market and the state.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
